BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Solar Observing Party *New Date*
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260908T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260908T163000
UID:6a7dfee92c859e0086ae839a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Astronomers from the Dunlap Institute for Astronomy & Astrophy
 sics will set up three types of telescopes: a visible-light telescope with
  a solar filter\, a specialized solar telescope with a hydrogen-alpha filt
 er and a Seestar telescope that displays a live image of the Sun on an iPa
 d. Participants will learn about solar viewing safety.\nOutdoor program. O
 pen to all ages of children. Younger children accompanied by caregivers.\n
 Drop-in\n*This is the rescheduled date!*\nLive or automated closed caption
 ing\, sign language interpretation\, intervenor services\, or attendant se
 rvices are available upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 w
 eeks in advance to: tpl.ca/accessibility-events.
LOCATION:Jones\, Parking lot behind Jones Branch
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7dfee92c859e0086ae839a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
